  "question": {
    "text": "The graph of the antiderivative of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></math> passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then the value of&nbsp;<math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "7",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let <math><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> represent the antiderivative of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‍</mi></math><br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">∫</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>⋅</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">‍</mi></math>…[integration by parts]<br />&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math><br />The graph of <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math> passes through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>e</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math><br />Hence,&nbsp;<math><mi>g</mi><mn>(</mn><mi>x</mi><mn>)</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi>e</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>g</mi><mn>(</mn><mi>x</mi><mn>)</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p>",
